  "Question": "Martians measure angles in clerts. There are \\(500\\) clerts in a full circle. How many clerts are there in a right angle?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(90\\)",
    "B": "\\(100\\)",
    "C": "\\(125\\)",
    "D": "\\(180\\)",
    "E": "\\(250\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Four equal right angles make a full circle. Therefore a right angle measures one fourth of the full circle, regardless of the angle unit used. In clerts, its measure is\n\\[500\\div4=125.\\]\nThe answer is \\(125\\) clerts, choice C.",
